    {
      "title": "Delegate RecipeImageManager web upload to XFileUploadHandler",
      "type": "tech-debt",
      "area": [
        "recipe"
      ],
      "priority": "Medium",
      "body": "## Finding\n`RecipeImageManager._uploadXFileWithWebSupport()` (line ~874) duplicates the exact same web/blob upload logic that exists in `XFileUploadHandler.uploadXFile()` (line ~156). Both check `kIsWeb || blob:`, read bytes, call `uploadImageFromBytes()`, with identical error handling.\n\nThe handler was extracted specifically for this purpose, but the manager retained its own copy.\n\n## Why It Matters\nAny future change to the web upload path must be made in two places. The duplication was introduced during the BUT-145 image pipeline fix and caught during /simplify review.\n\n## Suggested Fix\nInject or instantiate `XFileUploadHandler` in `RecipeImageManager` and delegate `_uploadXFileWithWebSupport` to `XFileUploadHandler.uploadXFile()`. Delete the private method. Requires updating RecipeImageManager's constructor/DI to accept the handler.\n\nFiles: `lib/viewmodels/recipe_form/recipe_image_manager.dart`, `lib/viewmodels/recipe_form/image_management/xfile_upload_handler.dart`"
    },
    {
      "title": "Optimize avatar compression dimensions to 400x400",
      "type": "performance",
      "area": [
        "account"
      ],
      "priority": "Low",
      "body": "## Finding\nAvatar uploads now go through `compressImageBytes()` with the default 1200x1200 max dimensions. Avatars are displayed at 48-128px in the app. Compressing to 1200x1200 is overkill and adds unnecessary latency � especially for large camera photos where the progressive quality loop (up to 4 iterations) may trigger.\n\n## Why It Matters\nUsers expect near-instant feedback after picking an avatar photo. For a 5MB camera photo, compression to 1200px can take 400ms-1.2s on mobile. Targeting 400x400 would produce much smaller output on the first pass and likely avoid the retry loop entirely, cutting compression time by ~60-75%.\n\n## Suggested Fix\nAdd optional `maxWidth`/`maxHeight` parameters to `StorageService.uploadImageBytes()` (or `ImageUploadService.uploadImageFromBytes()`), defaulting to 1200. Avatar callers pass 400. The `compressImageBytes()` method already accepts these parameters � just need to thread them through the service layers.\n\nFiles: `lib/services/storage_service.dart`, `lib/services/upload/image_upload_service.dart`, `lib/viewmodels/user_profile_viewmodel.dart`"
    },
    {
      "issueId": "BUT-276",
      "title": "Consolidate 3 duplicate shopping list export implementations",
      "description": "Three independent categorized export implementations exist for shopping lists. Should unify behind one shared implementation.\n\nLocations:\n1. shopping_list_management_module.dart:exportListAsText() � plain text with check marks\n2. personal_shopping_operations.dart:exportListAsText() � rich text with emojis\n3. ShoppingAnalyticsManager.exportListAsTextWithCategories() � emoji-based, takes itemsByCategory map\n4. ShoppingExportModule (shopping_share_operations.dart) � still a stub returning fake text\n\nAll share the same category-grouping loop (putIfAbsent, sort, iterate). Extract shared categorization logic and unify export formatting.",
      "labels": [
        "Code Quality",
        "Shopping"
      ],
      "priority": "Low"
    }
